[{:db/id "q-104782/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "cd250dfa-ca60-54a2-ab12-40e2e658bfa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "c62f9f05-3fba-546a-9ed3-c63c34d8c984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "77bd1567-ec27-5dc4-be74-7001e937903a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "4a8ea702-a177-50e0-9663-391e3ce7c672" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "86cae644-34bf-59b9-99b2-d6b752676a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0962a068-c807-584e-9232-cf2c4b1afafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104782/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-104782/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-104782/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-104782/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-104782/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-104782/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104782" :question/id #uuid "37afa10e-5c67-5b1e-ad86-c44cc76a4131" :question/math-academy-id "q-104782" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/2a11d5b84bdf66b6406f9465ba6a8bc8ecdf364bea2dcd6902034990a74ef0a9.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is given above. Find ${f}^{′}(-3).$" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${f}^{′}(-3),$ we need to find the slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ at $x=-3.$\n\nLet's consider the graph of $y=f(x)$ on $[-5,-2].$ Notice that $x=-3$ lies in this interval.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/59159512fa1b51477f171584a3717e2bf2774e8c940b59525fe478e1bcf6aece.png)\n\nThe slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in (-5,-2)$ is constant and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{1-4}{-2-(-5)}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(-3)=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104782/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a16e7b6-2a09-5aeb-9a8b-ea8fb1d59807"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "48bbff25-f78c-5cf6-9959-bc6e0902e482" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e7371afe-5750-5a7e-b179-e5701f8fbfba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "de431da7-a3de-5409-a626-2ffcc79dc041" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a692e996-3a60-5f66-89e1-9e59d2bc47a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3101713c-3ec7-5808-ac92-41fa98fb9710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d43708-64ed-5a56-9c46-95bab92ffbd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104784/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-104784/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-104784/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-104784/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-104784/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-104784/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104784" :question/id #uuid "6b828410-633b-56b5-9708-af2c0412ad03" :question/math-academy-id "q-104784" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/e5bcb5723747beb905cc93e3bcf8e3a5be7bf566cf408998d3173490bd2486b5.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find ${h}^{′}(-3)$ where $h(x)=-3f(x)-g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The addition and constant multiple rules for derivatives give\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=-3{f}^{′}(x)-{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(-3)=-3{f}^{′}(-3)-{g}^{′}(-3).\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that $x=-3$ corresponds to\n\n- the interval $x\\in (-5,-2)$ for the function $f,$ and\n\n- the interval $x\\in (-5,-1)$ for the function $g,$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/4f8b5f4c3a87f6cb1c346a4672df96a068d74690f0b7c9c6f9a77a9a3710a34a.png)\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-5,-2)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δf}{Δx}=\\frac{-1-3}{-2-(-5)}=-\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{′}(-3)=-\\frac{4}{3}.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ is constant on $x\\in (-5,-1)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δg}{Δx}=\\frac{4-4}{-1-(-5)}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${g}^{′}(-3)=0.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-3) & =-3{f}^{′}(-3)-{g}^{′}(-3) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{3})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104784/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeaff08f-f2c5-5e51-baca-988348852948"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "3d5a7c40-1962-5ef0-944d-1d3a9087c033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3ee6ba69-ae86-5147-b5fe-437b9bc6290a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "47900e39-52af-5f9e-a131-9a7553dac10c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5c9076bc-d400-5517-a80c-b0deb326ae89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "294c6ef3-3e63-52f0-958a-96a5c1c1347c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "770d388c-a58a-57b6-ae7b-66a20b7e87ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104795/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-104795/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-104795/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-104795/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-104795/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-104795/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104795" :question/id #uuid "4daf08f1-ddc5-57c5-bb35-3b3c140a8cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104795" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/61c9cb5fed816e028cf47e3d6b264a40a2fc4c04bc5d330e8662a8dfd8fa26e1.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find ${h}^{′}(2)$ where $h(x)=f(x)g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(2)={f}^{′}(2)\\cdot g(2)+f(2)\\cdot {g}^{′}(2).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(2)=4$ and $g(2)=3.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-2,4)$ equals $0.$ So, ${f}^{′}(2)=0.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-4,4)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${g}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & ={f}^{′}(2)\\cdot g(2)+f(2)\\cdot {g}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 3+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104795/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36b05580-d22b-5ac4-b8a3-cd8d9629ef74"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344894/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "805cb65d-8a23-5f86-a277-a5c8b0aa2eae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344894/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "238add62-4d3d-5bb2-b247-fbbd656e9249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344894/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "35629b96-66b9-51f6-8933-3f9798eb86c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344894/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-344894/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-344894/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344894" :question/id #uuid "15020dfc-75e9-546a-bdc3-2e8b45dfd09e" :question/math-academy-id "q-344894" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/bd78704be61e30879d4e659a255f93f5c8b6e560951d06b23cf547c8846b01ee.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=h(x)$ are given above. Find ${p}^{′}(2)$ where $p(x)=f(x)h(x).$\n\n${p}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{p}^{′}(x)={f}^{′}(x)\\cdot h(x)+f(x)\\cdot {h}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{p}^{′}(2)={f}^{′}(2)\\cdot h(2)+f(2)\\cdot {h}^{′}(2).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(2)=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $h(2)=0.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${f}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The slope of $h(x)$ on $x\\in (1,3)$ equals $2.$ So, ${h}^{′}(2)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(2) & ={f}^{′}(2)\\cdot h(2)+f(2)\\cdot {h}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot 0+(\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-344894/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36b05580-d22b-5ac4-b8a3-cd8d9629ef74"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-344914/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "18b53151-7834-5a3c-872e-ece384db61d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-344914/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "012c26aa-6f05-5865-a302-36f99157d46c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-344914/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer-field/choices ["q-344914/field-1/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-344914" :question/id #uuid "513f7389-d968-58ce-94d6-fe04861c05c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-344914" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947756/assets/f23d8acd8b59e630987fd9a04b71a5e0813f5c084f22489af342ba04c34eb003.png)\n\nGiven the plots of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ above, find ${h}^{′}(-1)$ where $h(x)=\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}.$\n\n${h}^{′}(-1)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\n{h}^{′}(-1)=\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(-1)=1$ and $g(-1)=2.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $f(x)$ on $x\\in (-3,1)$ equals $1.$ So, ${f}^{′}(-1)=1.$\n\n- The slope of $g(x)$ on $x\\in (-3,1)$ equals $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, ${g}^{′}(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-1) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)\\cdot g(-1)-f(-1)\\cdot {g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})}{(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-344914/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e274fe1-7242-5a6c-8351-eeff9877d2bf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-344914"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
